# Applied automatically to anyone using -lib hxscript.
#
# Between them these two are the whole of the setup. A build that adds `-lib hxscript` beside the
# game library it already had needs nothing else: the libraries in the build are detected, their
# packages are force-compiled, a bridge is generated per scriptable base, their abstracts are given
# a runtime form, and the matching runtime half is installed before the first script is parsed.
#
# See docs/embedding.md, and src/hxscript/setup/Autowire.hx for the defines that narrow or turn off
# any part of it.

# Keeps the standard-library types scripts reach by reflection. Dead code elimination decides what to
# strip by what the COMPILED code references, and a script references nothing at compile time, so
# under the default -dce std a member no call site happens to use is removed and a script reaching it
# finds a null field.
#
# -D hxscript_no_keep turns this off.
--macro hxscript.macro.Keep.run()

# The four setup steps, driven by which game libraries this build has. Runs inside
# onAfterInitMacros, so it does not matter whether -lib flixel comes before or after -lib hxscript.
#
# -D hxscript_no_autowire turns this off.
--macro hxscript.setup.Autowire.run()
